\lispPackageChapter{chorus}

Load this package with \texttt{(ql:quickload :chorus)}. It reexports the
generic backend interface from \texttt{chorus/backend}, the kernel language
from \texttt{chorus/lang}, the CUDA API from \texttt{chorus/api}, and two
driver variables from \texttt{chorus/driver-api}: \texttt{*show-messages*}
and \texttt{*sdk-not-found*}.

\texttt{*backend*} and \texttt{list-devices} are the calls most programs
make. \texttt{chorus/cuda} is the native CUDA package.
\texttt{chorus/apple-silicon} is the native Apple silicon package.

\texttt{*sdk-not-found*} is true when the CUDA driver library does not load.
Driver calls then signal \texttt{sdk-not-found-error}. Chorus also targets
Apple silicon and AMD GPUs.

The packages below are the ones \texttt{chorus} is built from. Use them when
you want a narrower set of symbols than the reexport.
